@startuml starchess-mode
' SPEC: _spec/apps/ui/starchess/starchess-mode.puml
' OUTDATED: Phase 5–6 — product lives in apps/starchess; Coach only redirects/nerd prompt.
' purpose: Product / UX mode — goals, specials, economy, UX v1.
!include ../../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title OUTDATED — StarChess Mode · Product / UX

package "Goals (vs classical chess)" {
  component "Turn structure — both sides queue,\nEnd / timeout submits" as G1 <<async>>
  component "Actions per turn — ≤1 special + ≤1 classical\n(stack order → B / F)" as G2 <<app>>
  component "Conflicts — classical = **attack** then **move**" as G3 <<app>>
  component "Economy — minerals + vespene" as G4 <<db>>
  component "Vision — cumulative fog (always on in mode)" as G5 <<db>>
  component "King — **3 lives**; may walk into fire;\nadjacent kings duel — mutual, **1 HP per checker**,\nequal HP ends 0/0 as a **draw**" as G6 <<app>>
}

package "Specials (product)" {
  component "Pawn — gas step (pawnDouble)\n+1 forward; stacks with classical" as S1 <<app>>
  component "Knight — Spider Mine (knightMine)\nM: overlay; cap 2 / side" as S2 <<app>>
  component "Bishop — Charon (bishopSnipe)\n2 gas; ignore blockers" as S3 <<app>>
  component "Rook — Siege toggle (rookSiege)\ntank ↔ siege vision / mobility" as S4 <<app>>
  component "Queen — Tactical Jump (queenWarp)\n2 gas; visible empty square" as S5 <<app>>
  component "King — Spawn\nadjacent deploy; can collide\nwith king-shots; a deploy on the enemy\nking's ring stacks a 2nd checker" as S6 <<app>>
}

package "UX (v1)" {
  component "ResourceBar + TurnBar\nabove the board; fog forced\nwhen ""starChessMode""" as U1 <<app>>
  component "Cumulative vision (""vision.ts"")\nunion of friendly units;\nmines light own square" as U2 <<db>>
  component "Attack-time reveal\nshooter ""from"" shown for the shot cue" as U3 <<app>>
  component "Fog-edge DualNav stories\n(Bishop / Rook tank) — SCFEN only;\nreview DualNav: observer dual-vision\n(""getSideVision"" w+b borders, no veil)" as U4 <<app>>
}

note bottom
  Long-press / GasDeploy queues ""B"" or ""F"" (stack order).
  Costs from the MODE economy — most specials **1** gas;
  Charon + Jump **2**.
  **Spider Mine combat:** path-chase / attack-mine; ignores allies
  + enemy kings (""mines.ts"" + ""resolveTurn"").
  **OUTDATED ownership:** not exclusive to Coach ""NerdScreen"".
  Live UI → ""apps/starchess"" (""/starchess/""); Coach keeps
  ""features/nerd"" + ""StarChessRedirect"" only.
  ====
  **Face-to-face kings (rules → resolve.puml).** Contact is **mutual and
  simultaneous**, and costs 1 HP **per checking unit**, so equal HP
  drains to 0/0 and the game is a **draw** (""scOutcome""). Because the King
  deploys onto its own adjacent ring, contact becomes a **deploy race** —
  a king that spawns a unit covering the enemy king chips 2 HP/turn while
  taking 1. Breaking contact still pays that turn's **parting shot**.
  ----
  **Known gaps (not shipped):** the ""GameOverBanner"" is still suppressed
  for StarChess in ""StarChessBoardView.tsx"", so a draw currently has **no
  banner**; ""StarChessState.winner"" (""types.ts"") remains **unused**.
  King adjacency via the board is unlocked by the SC movegen provider
  (sc-moves.puml) when a planning snap is live.
  ----
  **Pending UI (deferred — do not treat as shipped):**
  * **(a) deploy + move (spawn then C)** — broken in UI:
    ""useScMoveProvider"" destinations/commit read pre-B
    ""planningSnapshot.placement"", so a same-turn B=spawn
    unit cannot be selected/moved even though
    ""assertClassicalBaseline"" already accepts C.from =
    spawn.to. Engine path is fine; board provider is not.
  * **(b) siege tank mode + mode** — toggle UI (gas /
    mode chip / double-toggle affordance) is broken or
    unclear; engine ""rookSiege"" B/F + ""S:"" resolve is
    authoritative. Defer UI fix.
  ----
  **Pending product — fog / vision first-class:**
  * Cumulative fog is forced on in ""starChessMode"", but
    viewer-masked movegen, fog-faithful AI, and first-class
    vision UX (not only DualNav SCFEN samples) are **not**
    done. DualNav **review** now shows observer dual-vision
    borders (SCFEN ""getSideVision"" for both colors; full board).
    Live play remains single-viewer fog. ""scMoves"" still takes
    full occupancy; adjutant threat reads are full-board (only
    enemy-king hunt bonus is vision-gated). Track as pending,
    not regressions.
  ----
  **Queue edit:** TurnBar chips carry an X to
  ""removeQueuedScAction"" (refund special gas).
  Opponent planner: ""packages/starchess-core/ai/adjutant.ts"".
end note
@enduml
